ract_lead_info AFTER the lead has confirmed in a PREVIOUS message that what you spelled back is correct.\n3. **If they correct it**, spell the corrected version back again and confirm once more before saving.\n4. **Only after they confirm** — save the email and continue the conversation.\n\nNever skip this step, even if you are confident you heard it correctly.\nTOOL CALLING RULES — call tools silently in the background, never mention them in your spoken response:\n- extract_lead_info: Call IMMEDIATELY when the lead reveals their name, company, industry, timeline, budget, or decision-maker status. For contact_email or contact_phone: NEVER include these fields unless the lead ALREADY confirmed the spelled-out address in their PREVIOUS message. If the lead just said the email for the first time this turn, do NOT include it yet — wait until after you have read it back and they said yes in a later message.\n- capture_pain_point: Call ONCE — the first time the lead clearly describes their core business problem. Do NOT call again if you have already called this tool earlier in the conversation, even if the lead adds detail, repeats the pain, or you are batching it with other tools like score_lead.\n- detect_objection: Call immediately when the lead expresses hesitation, price concern, need for approval, or doubt about moving forward.\n- score_lead + recommend_offer: These two tools MUST always fire TOGETHER in the same turn — include both in a single response. Call score_lead once Phase 3 is complete (pain point known + at least 2 of: timeline, decision-maker, budget readiness). Always call recommend_offer in the exact same batch, never separately or in a later turn.\n- book_discovery_call: Call when the lead is Hot or Warm and explicitly agrees to book a call.\n- generate_follow_up: Call at the very end of the conversation before saying goodbye.\nYou may call multiple tools in a single turn. Never narrate or describe tool calls in your spoken response.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Nice to meet you, David! What kind of business do you run?'}, {'content': ' Um, I run a logistics company called FastCargo.', 'role': 'user'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Great to know, David! What's the biggest challenge you're facing in your business right now?"}, {'content': " We've been losing over the past, uh, we've been losing a lot of customers over the past few months, and I don't know how to stop it.", 'role': 'user'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'That sounds challenging, David. How long has this been an issue for you?'}, {'content': " Um, we've been losing customers over the past few months, and I don't know how to stop it.", 'role': 'user'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I understand, David. How is this affecting your day-to-day operations?'}, {'content': " Um, about 3 months now, and it's really hurting us. So yeah, we've been losing a lot of revenue.", 'role': 'user'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'It sounds like a significant concern, David. How soon are you hoping to solve this — this month, this quarter, or later?'}, {'content': ' Um, yeah, probably later. I, I mean, not later, uh, probably this quarter.', 'role': 'user'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_DOnlBOC7CYwlFtGBHbme0Pqo', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'extract_lead_info', 'arguments': '{"contact_name":"David","company":"FastCargo","timeline":"this quarter"}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_DOnlBOC7CYwlFtGBHbme0Pqo', 'content': '{"ok": true, "updated_fields": {"company": "FastCargo", "timeline": "this quarter", "name": "David"}}'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'max_tokens': 500, 'stream': True}}
