 the dot" / "no dot" / "no period" → remove all `.` from the local part (before the @)\n   - "all one word" / "no spaces" → remove spaces and separators\n   - "underscore instead of hyphen" → replace `-` with `_`\n   - Numbers spoken as words → convert to digits ("twenty" → "20", "four" → "4")\n\n1. **Spell back the NORMALIZED version** segment by segment using these spoken forms:\n   - `.` in the local part → say "dot"  |  `-` → "hyphen"  |  `_` → "underscore"  |  `@` → "at"\n   - Read each contiguous segment as a **single whole unit** — do NOT split or add spaces inside a word (e.g., "batubata" → say "batubata", NOT "batu bata" or "batu bato")\n   - Example A — no correction given: Lead says "batubata.david20@gmail.com" → You say: "Let me read that back — batubata dot david twenty at gmail dot com. Did I get that right?"\n   - Example B — with correction: Lead says "batu-bato.david20@gmail.com without the hyphen and without the dot" → normalize to batubatodavid20@gmail.com → You say: "Let me read that back — batubatodavid twenty at gmail dot com. Did I get that right?"\n\n2. **Wait for confirmation.** Do NOT include the email in any tool call on the same turn you first heard it. Only add it to extract_lead_info AFTER the lead has confirmed in a PREVIOUS message that what you spelled back is correct.\n\n3. **If they correct it**, apply their new corrections, spell the updated version back, and confirm once more before saving.\n\n4. **Only after they confirm** — save the normalized email and continue the conversation.\n\nNever skip step 0. Never read back the raw transcribed version if the lead gave corrections.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Hello, David! It seems there's a little confusion with the call."}, {'content': ' Kaya nga, yun yung problema, hindi ko ma-choose.', 'role': 'user'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I see, David. It sounds like decision-making is quite a challenge for you right now. Can you tell me how long this has been an issue for you?'}, {'content': ' Na-interrupt siya, kaya hindi na.', 'role': 'user'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I understand that interruptions can be frustrating. Let’s focus on how we can address your decision-making challenges. How is this affecting your day-to-day operations?'}, {'content': " Product list. Stop, stop. 'Di ba? Ang na-interrupt yun eh. Sino?  Finish ko na yung—", 'role': 'user'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "I see you're trying to clarify. Let's get back on track. What's the biggest challenge you're facing in your business right now?"}, {'content': ' Pa kami.  Huwag niyo naman yung sayo sa yung sa documentation, ibang Mac niya. Alam niyo na. Ako, maggagawa ako ng bagong for B2C.  Wait lang, ito na. Ico-commit ko pa lang eh.', 'role': 'user'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Got it, David. It sounds like you're in the process of creating something new for B2C. Can you share what specific challenges you're encountering with that?"}, {'content': ' Gawin na, using yung mga niyo.', 'role': 'user'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_RqZ4DNfIQUttAvE6JRTX4og2', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'no_op', 'arguments': '{}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_RqZ4DNfIQUttAvE6JRTX4og2', 'content': '{"ok": true}'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'max_tokens': 500, 'stream': True}}
